# Obsidian local workplace states & caches
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/workspace*
.obsidian/cache/
.obsidian/indexed*

# 🤖 Local AI Indices & Plugin Caches
.smart-env/
.claudian/

# 🔒 SECRETS & SENSITIVE KEYS (NEVER COMMIT TO GIT)
.secrets/
00-Private/
*.env
*.env.*
*_secret*
*_private*

# System files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Logs & temp
*.log

# 📓 PERSONAL CONTENT (the system is shareable, the journal is not)
# History audit found 8 daily notes had been committed and later deleted —
# deletion does not remove them from history, so these rules make the boundary
# structural instead of relying on never typing `git add -A`.
# MOCs and already-tracked showcase files stay tracked; everything else is isolated.

01-Daily/*
!01-Daily/_*.md
!01-Daily/Habit Analytics Dashboard.md

02-Projects/*
!02-Projects/_*.md
!02-Projects/weather-dashboard/

03-Dev/*
!03-Dev/_*.md

04-Learning/*
!04-Learning/_*.md

05-Personal/*
!05-Personal/_*.md

07-Reviews/*
!07-Reviews/_*.md

99-Attachments/*
!99-Attachments/_*.md
!99-Attachments/2026-08/obsidian-*.png
!99-Attachments/2026-08/file-20260803003355764.png

# Quick captures are a live feed of raw thoughts — dashboards only.
00-Inbox/*
!00-Inbox/_*.md

# The example env file MUST ship — README's setup step is `cp .env.example .env`.
# Without this negation the `*.env.*` rule above silently swallows it, and a
# fresh clone arrives with no template to copy.
!.env.example
